Subject: [PATCH 39/42] drivers/pc80/rtc: Start each boot's CMOS POST bank with
 a POST code

With CMOS_POST, cmos_post_init() switches to the other of two CMOS
banks at every boot, and the next boot reports the last POST code and
extra log of that bank when they do not end a boot normally. Until the
first POST code of the boot is written, the bank still holds the codes
of the boot before the previous one. A boot that stops before its first
POST code, for example an S3 resume that hangs in the bootblock or
early in romstage, is then reported with the codes of an older boot,
usually ones that end a boot normally, and the hang goes unnoticed.

Write POSTCODE_BOOTBLOCK_CAR and clear the extra log as soon as the
bank is selected.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541. Not tested on hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c b/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c
index 8150fbad8..ca5300534 100644
--- a/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c
+++ b/src/drivers/pc80/rtc/post.c
@@ -92,6 +92,14 @@ void cmos_post_init(void)
 	}
 
 	cmos_write(magic, CMOS_POST_BANK_OFFSET);
+
+	/*
+	 * The bank still holds the codes of the boot before the previous one.
+	 * Replace them now: a boot that stops before its first POST code must
+	 * not be reported with the codes of an older boot.
+	 */
+	cmos_post_code(POSTCODE_BOOTBLOCK_CAR);
+	cmos_post_extra(0);
 }
 
 void cmos_post_code(u8 value)
